# Reviewed exemptions for the credential sweep that scans this repository.
#
# HOW IT IS READ. A credential sweep checks this repo and fails on any finding. It considers
# every TRACKED path, deliberately: a `.gitignore` rule does not untrack an already-tracked
# file, so a path that gitignore-aware tools skip can still be sitting in the tree.
#
# FORMAT, one per line:   <path or shell glob> | <reason this is not a credential>
#
# The REASON IS MANDATORY - an entry with nothing after the `|` is reported as a finding in
# its own right. A bare path list is how an exemption outlives the thing that justified it.
#
# A per-line `allow-secret` in a comment is honoured too and is preferred where it fits: a
# file entry silently stops policing everything else in that file, and leaks arrive one line
# at a time. This file is for the case where the whole file's job is credential patterns.
#
# NOT FOR A REAL CREDENTIAL. `git rm --cached` and rotate it at the vendor - removing the
# file does not invalidate the value, and this repo is PUBLIC.

src/utils/redact.test.ts | the redaction engine's own unit test: every value in it is a synthetic vendor-shaped fixture asserted to be MASKED, so the file is credential-shaped by construction. No live counterpart exists.
